{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "355ede48-dc88-44e4-823f-9c226c6a0a85",
    "name": "MediBridge API",
    "description": "MediBridge — Secure AI-Assisted Clinical Document Exchange.\n\nEndpoints pulled from the capstone proposal + the full endpoint list in the Role Assignment doc. Request bodies use IDs and enum values from database/seed_data.sql (Raissa — Engineer 5) so you can run these against a locally-seeded database with no edits.\n\nEnum values (source of truth, confirmed against seed_data.sql):\n- status: uploaded, ocr_complete, classified, routed, delivered, rejected, ocr_failed\n- document_type: referral, lab_result, discharge_summary, insurance_form, imaging\n- priority: urgent, normal, routine\n- role: organization_admin, provider, registered_nurse, referral_coordinator, medical_assistant (finalized by Olga on Slack — replaces earlier physician/admin/specialist placeholders)\n\nEdge-case docs added for error-handling / filtering tests (see 'Error Handling & Edge Cases' folder):\n- TX-1011 (doc_rejected_id) — status=rejected, recipient rejected as duplicate\n- TX-1012 (doc_ocr_failed_id) — status=ocr_failed, document_text.ocr_status=failed\n- TX-1013 (doc_permission_denied_id) — routed to Metro General only; a St. Mercy user's access attempt is denied (see audit_event_auth_failure_id)\n\n---\nUPDATED on 08/04/2026 after QA audit (compared against api/routes/*.py and the production openapi.json - https://app.medibridge.click):\n- Fixed /ai/analysis -> /ai/analyses (2 requests)\n- Added 24 endpoints that existed in the backend but weren't covered: Dashboard (4), AI stats/categories (2), Documents download-url/read (2), Organizations update (1), Notifications delete (1), Security (2), Notification Preferences (2), API Keys (3), Webhooks (3), Tasks (3), Internal AI (1 happy path + 1 negative case)\n- 'Register' kept intentionally as a test case documenting that the endpoint doesn't exist (404 expected) - see Auth folder\n- See MediBridge_QA_Test_Plan.md and MediBridge_QA_Execution_Report.md for the full rationale behind each change",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "57130378",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/57130378-355ede48-dc88-44e4-823f-9c226c6a0a85?source=collection_link"
  },
